==========================================================================================================================
L18 -- the hydrostatic mass bias b propagated through L7 (the cosmic ratio) and L2 (the impossibility)
==========================================================================================================================

  the measured hydrostatic bias, M_HSE = (1-b) M_true:
      b = +0.03   X-COP, median of the sample (Ettori & Eckert 2022, A&A 657 L1)
      b = +0.17   X-COP, 80th percentile of the sample (Ettori & Eckert 2022)
      b = +0.15   X-COP gas-fraction SZ calibration 1-b = 0.85 +/- 0.05 (Eckert+2019 A&A 621 A40)
      b = +0.22   CCCP weak lensing, 1-b = 0.78 +/- 0.09 (Hoekstra+2015)
      b = +0.20   local cluster population median (Ettori & Eckert 2022)
      b = +0.20   FLAMINGO simulations at R500c, cluster scale (Kugel+2024)
      b = +0.31   Weighing the Giants weak lensing, 1-b = 0.69 +/- 0.07 (von der Linden+2014)
      b = +0.33   local cluster population 80th percentile (Ettori & Eckert 2022)
      b = +0.42   Planck 2015 XXIV counts-vs-CMB, 1-b ~ 0.58 (an upper envelope, not a measurement of b)
      ADOPTED measured range b in [0.00, 0.42]; X-COP's own sample b in [0.03, 0.17]; single-cluster empirical floor b = -0.20

  inputs: 248 corrected X-COP rows, 12 clusters, radii [30, 40, 50, 75, 100, 150, 200, 300, 420, 750, 1000] kpc; source closure_2026/cluster_measurement_audit_2026/results.json

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1.  L7 UNDER A CONSTANT BIAS.  Only g_HSE moves: g_true = g_HSE/(1-b).  g_bar (X-ray emission measure +
      stellar profile) and therefore s, M_bar and M_kernel do not depend on the temperature GRADIENT and are
      untouched.  f_bar = M_bar/M_true = (1-b) f_bar(b=0): a positive bias pushes f_bar DOWN, away from cosmic.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

