    the direction, stated as an identity: f_bar(b) = (1-b) f_bar(0) and M_dark/M_bar(b) = [1 + M_dark/M_bar(0)]/(1-b) - 1.
    So a positive b moves f_bar DOWN, AWAY from the cosmic 0.156, and moves the Newtonian ratio UP, away from
    5.43 -- but it moves both INTO the depletion band L7 itself allowed.  L7's R1 was written around 'clusters
    retain 70-100% of the cosmic baryon share at R500'; at b = 0 these twelve retain 96%, the very top of
    that window, and b = 0.20 brings them to 76%, its middle.  Read as a physical statement the bias
    therefore makes the cosmic-share reading MORE self-consistent; read as L7's literal numerical coincidence
    with 5.43 it degrades it, and check H6 below finds where the band is left.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  2.  RADIAL DEPENDENCE.  Three models the literature supports, all evaluated at L7's radius 0.80 R500.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    (i)   X-COP-anchored power law b(r) = b500 (r/R500)^beta with beta = 1.26 from the measured 6%->10%
          non-thermal fraction between R500 and R200 (Eckert+2019).  At 0.80 R500 it gives b = 0.755 b500,
          i.e. the radial form REDUCES the bias at L7's radius relative to R500 -- the direction adverse to this lane.
    (ii)  Nelson+2014 fraction through the exact gradient relation, dlnP_th/dlnr = -2.0: b(0.80 R500) = 0.122, b(R500) = 0.134, b(1.5 R500) = 0.183
    (ii)  Nelson+2014 fraction through the exact gradient relation, dlnP_th/dlnr = -3.0: b(0.80 R500) = 0.154, b(R500) = 0.178, b(1.5 R500) = 0.248
    (ii)  Nelson+2014 fraction through the exact gradient relation, dlnP_th/dlnr = -4.0: b(0.80 R500) = 0.170, b(R500) = 0.198, b(1.5 R500) = 0.277
          (sanity: at dlnP = -3 the value b(0.8 R500) = 0.154 sits below X-COP's 80th-percentile bound
          b < 0.17 but well above its median b < 0.03 (Ettori & Eckert 2022), i.e. the simulation-based profile is at
          the PESSIMISTIC end for this sample -- the direction adverse to this lane, which is why it is carried.
          Setting b = f_nth outright would give 0.213, which the lead's audit correctly warns against.)

