  3.  L2 UNDER A BIAS.  The required boost is Delta_req(s) = (g_true - g_bar)/a0 = (g_HSE/(1-b) - g_bar)/a0
      at s = g_bar/a0, which is unchanged.  The galaxy side (SPARC rotation curves) carries no hydrostatic
      assumption at all, so it does not move: the bias acts on ONE side of L2's comparison only.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    SPARC: 144 galaxies, 2681 points (Q<3, i>30, eV/V<0.10) -- the same cut L2 uses

