    the same in words: at b = 0 clusters need 2.2-5.1x the galaxy boost; at the population
    median b = 0.20 they need 2.9-6.5x; at the Weighing-the-Giants b = 0.31 they need 3.4-7.7x.
    The fitted log-slope moves from p = 0.811 to 0.818 to 0.821: the bias pushes p TOWARDS 1,
    which is exactly the 'constant rescaling of G, i.e. extra mass tracing the baryons' end of L2's C9 and
    further from the 1/2 that caps a kernel with a deep-MOND limit.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  4.  THE KEY QUESTION: SOLVE FOR THE b THAT WOULD RESCUE THE FRAMEWORK, then lay it beside the measured range.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    (a)  L7's residual to zero at 0.80 R500.  Requires  g_HSE/(1-b) = g_bar + a0 Delta(g_bar/a0)  at that radius.
         alt      : b_required = -0.681   (1-b = 1.681, i.e. M_HSE would have to OVER-state the true mass by 68%)
                    at that b, f_bar = 0.250 (161% of cosmic) and M_dark/M_bar = 3.00 vs cosmic 5.43
                    -- a SECOND cost, independent of any bias measurement: at the b the framework needs, all
                    twelve would hold 161% of the universal baryon share.  The lead's CLUSTER_AUDIT.md correctly
